<main>
<section class="hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">Verified owner evidence · 28 October 2026</div><h1>Recovery completed.<br>Evidence still decides.</h1><p class="lead">V132 finished the registered study and issued current reference forecasts. Numerical success did not create a qualified predictive edge.</p><div class="hero-note fine"><strong>Actual V132 owner: SUCCESS.</strong> All 24 study units are complete; all four historical qualification gates failed. V133 owner execution remains pending. Every result below retains its release, purpose and evidence boundary.</div></div><aside class="progressbox" aria-label="Registered study progress"><div class="eyebrow">Accepted study units</div><div class="count">24 <span>/ 24</span></div><div class="meter" role="progressbar" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="24" aria-valuenow="24" aria-label="Accepted training units"><i style="width:100%"></i></div><p>11 remaining units completed.</p><small>13 retained + 11 new units.<br>New work: 10 optimizer fits + 1 certified zero-call endpoint. 26 cumulative attempts; both earlier failures preserved.</small></aside></section>
<section class="statusgrid" aria-label="Independent actual owner statuses"><article class="card"><div class="statushead"><span class="eyebrow">01 · Research</span><span class="badge good">COMPLETE</span></div><h3>Recovered; no model qualified</h3><p class="fine">Eleven new units passed unchanged numerical acceptance. The complete historical family failed all four qualification gates. NFL annual-origin gains reversed in 2025; fixed-origin gains remained unqualified.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="statushead"><span class="eyebrow">02 · Forecast serving</span><span class="badge good">ISSUED</span></div><h3>83 MARKET-reference games</h3><p class="fine">29 NFL and 54 FBS references were issued at 20:20:13.969555 UTC on October 28, before the remaining research. No qualified learned-model forecasts. This is a dated snapshot.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="statushead"><span class="eyebrow">03 · Financial reporting</span><span class="badge good">COMPLETE</span></div><h3>Zero qualified executions</h3><p class="fine">Selective NFL-8/FBS-9 allocation $0; $500 unspent. Inherited conditional +$2.40 equals MARKET and is not actual profit. Reporting completion does not imply an executable order or fill.</p></article></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="results-title"><div class="sectiontitle"><div><div class="eyebrow">Compare like with like</div><h2 id="results-title">Historical research & reconstructed monitoring</h2></div><p class="fine muted">Choose one release, league, season and protocol. Missing panels stay missing. Lower log loss and Brier are better; neither proves profitability.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="controls"><label>Evidence release<select id="release"><option>V132</option><option>V131</option><option>V129</option></select></label><label>League<select id="league"><option>FBS</option><option>NFL</option></select></label><label>Season<select id="season"><option value="2024">2024–2025</option><option value="2025">2025–2026</option><option value="2026">2026–2027</option></select></label><label>Protocol<select id="policy"><option value="annual">Annual origin</option><option value="fixed">Fixed origin</option></select></label><label>Score<select id="metric"><option value="win_logloss">Log loss</option><option value="win_brier">Brier score</option></select></label></div><div id="results" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="caution">MARKET = archived sportsbook consensus, not a model, Kalshi or Polymarket executable quote. An exact-cohort numerical minimum is descriptive. Historical panels were repeatedly inspected. Current-season results cannot select a champion, calibration, features or staking policy. No forecast issue vintage is inferred from this aggregate export.</p></div></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="demo-title"><div class="sectiontitle"><div><div class="eyebrow">Executable architecture</div><h2 id="demo-title">Let one stage fail. Inspect the others.</h2></div><p class="fine muted">Every number below is invented. Scenario outputs come from the tested Python workflow. This demonstrates exception isolation. Actual V132 serving evidence is reported separately above.</p></div><div class="demo"><div class="eyebrow">Synthetic / offline / no orders</div><h3>A frozen policy is independent of a new experiment</h3><div class="buttons" role="group" aria-label="Invented failure scenarios"><button data-scenario="research_failure" aria-pressed="true">Research rejects</button><button data-scenario="research_complete" aria-pressed="false">Research completes</button><button data-scenario="stale_reference" aria-pressed="false">Reference is stale</button><button data-scenario="future_reference" aria-pressed="false">Reference is from the future</button></div><div id="demo-output" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="fine muted">The same frozen MARKET policy is retained in every scenario. Reference serving independently rejects invalid probabilities, future observations, started games, duplicates and outcome fields. These examples do not establish model edge or venue eligibility. Process death and memory exhaustion require a separate supervisor.</p></div></section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="recovery-title"><div class="sectiontitle"><div><div class="eyebrow">Durable stage boundaries · invented example</div><h2 id="recovery-title">Resume research. Reuse the delivered outputs.</h2></div><p class="fine muted">Eight stages, a bounded attempt journal and immutable accepted receipts. The public example writes real local files using invented inputs. Select each execution to inspect what runs again.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="buttons" id="recovery-controls" role="group" aria-label="Recoverable stage executions"><button data-recovery="first" aria-pressed="true">1 · Research fails</button><button data-recovery="resume" aria-pressed="false">2 · Resume failed research</button><button data-recovery="reentry" aria-pressed="false">3 · Reenter unchanged</button></div><div id="recovery-output" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="caution">A reused stage does no new work. Accepted forecast and financial identities remain exact across all three runs. Numerically accepted invented research still does not qualify a model or alter the frozen policy. The trusted local journal detects corruption and input changes; it is not a signed evidence store or distributed scheduler.</p><a href="../RECOVERABLE_OPERATIONS.md">Inspect the stage contracts and recovery limits →</a></div></section>
<section class="section split" aria-label="Numerical recovery and measured resources"><article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Numerical recovery is now observed</div><h2>Unchanged tolerance. Stronger evidence.</h2><div class="gap" aria-label="Maximum newly accepted gap1.3883729284283598e-8; unchanged limit2e-8"><div>Maximum accepted gap<i style="height:77.75px;background:var(--teal)"></i><span>1.3884 × 10⁻⁸</span></div><div class="limit">Unchanged limit<i style="height:112px"></i><span>2.0000 × 10⁻⁸</span></div></div><p class="fine">All 11 new V132 units completed. Independent review replayed 22 saved certificate calculations exactly and preserved all 13 prior payloads and 15 prior attempts. The bound remained 2 × 10⁻⁸.</p><p class="fine muted">Verification is conditional on saved diagnostic quantities; original rowwise derivatives were not reconstructed. The old rejected V131 iterate was not saved. V132 certifies newly computed iterates, not a retroactive success for that failure.</p></article><article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Measured V132 owner execution</div><h2>Work completed, limits respected.</h2><dl class="facts"><dt>Owner checks / required notebooks</dt><dd>3,025 passed / 4 passed</dd><dt>Supervisor / worker</dt><dd>620.474 / 576.876 s</dd><dt>Peak process-tree RSS</dt><dd>4.137 GB</dd><dt>Working disk</dt><dd>3.915 GB</dd><dt>New units / optimizer calls</dt><dd>11 / 10</dd><dt>Study units / total attempts</dt><dd>24 / 26</dd><dt>Historical qualification gates</dt><dd>0 / 4 passed</dd><dt>V133 owner execution</dt><dd>PENDING</dd></dl><p class="fine muted">Decimal GB. Observed owner runtime, not a throughput forecast. Successful numerical training and issued reference forecasts do not establish a learned-market or financial advantage.</p></article></section>
<section class="section"><div class="sectiontitle"><div><div class="eyebrow">Dated operational evidence</div><h2>One issue. Three native-week cohorts.</h2></div><p class="fine muted">All 83 selected references equal MARKET exactly and were issued before kickoff. No individual football forecasts or venue prices are published here.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>League / native week</th><th class="num">Distinct games</th><th>Issue, UTC</th><th>Selected policy</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>NFL 2026 week 8</td><td class="num">14</td><td>2026-10-28 20:20:13.969555</td><td>MARKET reference</td></tr><tr><td>NFL 2026 week 9</td><td class="num">15</td><td>Same issue</td><td>MARKET reference</td></tr><tr><td>FBS 2026 week 9</td><td class="num">54</td><td>Same issue</td><td>MARKET reference</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="fine muted">Source snapshot: 20:16:16.640545 UTC; input cutoff: 20:20:00.087384 UTC, October 28. The 8,718 separate research-probability rows span multiple models and are not 8,718 games or qualified serving outputs. Original native-week financial commitments were preserved. No current timestamp is inferred from opening this page.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="sectiontitle"><div><div class="eyebrow">Trace the claim</div><h2>Evidence you can inspect</h2></div></div><div class="sourcegrid"><article class="card"><h3>Actual owner aggregates</h3><p><a href="../evidence/2026-10-28-v132-execution.json">V132 complete owner & exact panels</a></p><p><a href="../evidence/2026-10-28-v131-execution.json">Preserved V131 failed execution</a></p><p><a href="../evidence/2026-10-28-v129-execution.json">V129 historical & monitoring baseline</a></p></article><article class="card"><h3>Run the mechanisms</h3><p><a href="../../examples/review_lab/recoverable_stages.py">Eight-stage recovery journal</a></p><p><a href="../../examples/review_lab/fault_isolation.py">Fault-isolation Python example</a></p><p><a href="../NUMERICAL_RECOVERY_INCIDENT.md">Numerical acceptance & recovery</a></p></article><article class="card"><h3>Keep the scope visible</h3><p><a href="../HISTORICAL_SELECTION_BOUNDARY.md">Historical selection boundary</a></p><p><a href="../BASKETBALL_MARKET_COVERAGE.md">Separate basketball evidence</a></p></article></div></section>
</main><footer>Sports Edge Lab · Public aggregate review · Self-contained; no network requests, tracking, credentials, private observations or individual football forecasts. Download this HTML and open it in a browser; GitHub's file viewer displays source.<noscript> JavaScript is required for comparisons and invented scenarios. The status summary and linked JSON evidence remain available.</noscript></footer>
<script id="dashboard-data" type="application/json">__DASHBOARD_DATA__</script>
<script>
'use strict';
const DATA=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('dashboard-data').textContent);
const esc=x=>String(x??'Unavailable').replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
const num=(x,d=6)=>x==null?'Unavailable':Number(x).toFixed(d);
function selectedRows(data,filter){return data.rows.filter(r=>r.release===filter.release&&r.league===filter.league&&r.season===Number(filter.season)&&r.policy===filter.policy);}
function resultView(data,filter){
 const rows=selectedRows(data,filter),monitor=Number(filter.season)===2026;
 const boundary=monitor&&filter.release==='V132'?'MONITORING ONLY · Reconstructed post-freeze V132 evaluation; not independently archived pregame performance. No ranking or selection.':monitor?'MONITORING ONLY · Retained V129 snapshot; not fresh V131 or V132 output. No current-season ranking or selection.':'HISTORICAL RESEARCH · Repeatedly exposed saved probabilities. Numerical comparisons do not replace complete qualification.';
 let out='<div class="banner '+(monitor?'monitor':'')+'">'+esc(boundary)+'</div>';
 if(!rows.length)return out+'<div class="empty"><h3>No saved panel for this selection</h3><p>'+esc(filter.release==='V132'?'V132 monitoring is annual-origin only; fixed-origin current panels are not published.':filter.release==='V131'?(monitor?'V131 reached no new 2026 monitoring or serving stage.':'The failed V131 run retained FBS panels only; no NFL heldout panel is available.'):'This compact V129 export provides annual historical and retained monitoring aggregates only.')+'</p><p class="fine">Missing evidence is not a zero score. Change the filters to inspect an available panel.</p></div>';
 const m=filter.metric,market=rows.find(r=>r.model.startsWith('MARKET reference')),reference=market[m],best=Math.min(...rows.map(r=>r[m]));
 const maxDelta=Math.max(0.000001,...rows.map(r=>Math.abs(r[m]-reference)));
 out+='<div class="comparison"><div><div class="eyebrow">Matched MARKET reference</div><div class="score">'+num(reference)+'</div><p class="fine">'+esc(m==='win_logloss'?'Log loss':'Brier score')+' · '+rows[0].games+' games · '+esc(filter.league)+'</p><p class="fine muted">'+esc(rows[0].origin.replaceAll('_',' '))+'<br>'+esc(monitor?'Retained forward evaluation; no promotion.':filter.release==='V131'?'Full study qualification: INCOMPLETE.':'Completed study: all four qualification gates FAILED.')+'</p></div><div class="chart">';
 if(monitor){out+='<div class="banner monitor">Operational serving remains MARKET. Research monitoring scores never choose the policy. No outcome-based highlight, rank or winner is assigned.</div>';}else{
  out+='<div class="eyebrow">Difference from MARKET · '+esc(m==='win_logloss'?'log loss':'Brier')+'</div>';
  for(const r of rows){const delta=r[m]-reference,w=Math.abs(delta)/maxDelta*47;out+='<div class="chartrow"><span>'+esc(r.model)+'</span><span class="track"><i class="zero"></i><i class="bar '+(delta<0?'better':'')+'" style="left:'+(delta<0?50-w:50)+'%;width:'+w+'%"></i></span><span>'+ (delta>0?'+':'')+num(delta)+'</span></div>';}
  out+='<div class="axis"><span>← lower / better</span><span>higher / worse →</span></div>';
 }
 out+='</div></div><div class="scroll"><table><caption class="sr-only">Exact selected aggregate panel; unavailable metrics are explicit</caption><thead><tr><th>Model / reference</th><th class="num">Games</th><th class="num">'+esc(m==='win_logloss'?'Log loss':'Brier')+'</th><th class="num">ECE10</th><th class="num">Correct / incorrect</th><th>Paired Δ log loss 95% interval</th></tr></thead><tbody>';
 for(const r of rows){out+='<tr><td>'+esc(r.model)+'</td><td class="num">'+r.games+'</td><td class="num '+(!monitor&&r[m]===best?'best':'')+'">'+num(r[m])+'</td><td class="num">'+num(r.ece10)+'</td><td class="num">'+(r.correct==null?'Unavailable':r.correct+' / '+r.incorrect)+'</td><td>'+(r.delta_ci95?'['+num(r.delta_ci95[0])+', '+num(r.delta_ci95[1])+']':'Not in this export')+'</td></tr>';}
 out+='</tbody></table></div><p class="fine muted">'+(monitor?'No rankings on the current-season monitoring view.':'Emphasis marks the numerical minimum only within this exact panel. Intervals are descriptive saved native-week comparisons. Complete historical qualification remains a separate decision.')+'</p>';
 return out;
}
function demoView(data,name){const x=data.scenarios[name];let out='<div class="lanes">';for(const [label,state] of [['1 · New research',x.research],['2 · Frozen reference serving',x.serving],['3 · Paper readiness',x.execution]])out+='<div class="lane"><h3>'+label+'</h3><span class="badge '+(state.status==='FAILED'?'bad':state.status==='SERVED'||state.status==='COMPLETED'?'good':'neutral')+'">'+esc(state.status)+'</span><p class="fine">'+esc(state.status==='FAILED'?'Ordinary research exception captured.':state.status==='COMPLETED'?'Research completed; frozen policy unchanged.':state.status==='SERVED'?'Two invented reference forecasts produced.':state.status==='BLOCKED'?'Reference validation failed independently.':'No qualified edge or executable venue evidence.')+'</p></div>';out+='</div><div class="trace">'+esc('01 research → '+x.research.status+'\n02 reference validation → '+x.serving.status+'\n03 forecasts in invented output → '+x.serving.forecasts.length+'\n04 paper stake → $0; actual orders → 0; profit → unavailable\nFrozen policy identity → '+(x.serving.policy_sha256||'not served'))+'</div>';
 if(x.serving.forecasts.length){out+='<div class="scroll"><table><caption class="sr-only">Invented example output, not football forecasts</caption><thead><tr><th>Invented fixture</th><th class="num">Reference probability</th><th>Classification</th><th>Learned edge</th></tr></thead><tbody>';for(const r of x.serving.forecasts)out+='<tr><td>'+esc(r.game)+'</td><td class="num">'+num(r.probability,2)+'</td><td>Invented MARKET reference</td><td>Unavailable</td></tr>';out+='</tbody></table></div>';}
 return out;
}
function update(){const filter={};for(const id of ['release','league','season','policy','metric'])filter[id]=document.getElementById(id).value;document.getElementById('results').innerHTML=resultView(DATA,filter);}
for(const id of ['release','league','season','policy','metric'])document.getElementById(id).addEventListener('change',update);
for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-scenario]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{for(const other of document.querySelectorAll('[data-scenario]'))other.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(other===b));document.getElementById('demo-output').innerHTML=demoView(DATA,b.dataset.scenario);});
update();document.getElementById('demo-output').innerHTML=demoView(DATA,'research_failure');
function recoveryView(data,name){const r=data.recovery[name];let out='<div class="comparison"><div><div class="eyebrow">New stage attempts</div><div class="score">'+r.new_attempts+'</div></div><div><div class="eyebrow">Accepted stages reused</div><div class="score">'+r.reused_stages+'</div></div></div><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Outcome</th><th>New work</th><th>Output identity prefix</th></tr></thead><tbody>';for(const x of r.stages)out+='<tr><td>'+esc(x.stage.replaceAll('_',' '))+'</td><td><span class="badge '+(x.status==='FAILED'?'bad':x.status==='BLOCKED'?'neutral':'good')+'">'+esc(x.status)+'</span></td><td>'+String(x.executed)+'</td><td><code>'+esc(x.output_sha256?x.output_sha256.slice(0,16):'No accepted output')+'</code></td></tr>';return out+'</tbody></table></div>';}
for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-recovery]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{for(const other of document.querySelectorAll('[data-recovery]'))other.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(other===b));document.getElementById('recovery-output').innerHTML=recoveryView(DATA,b.dataset.recovery);});
document.getElementById('recovery-output').innerHTML=recoveryView(DATA,'first');
globalThis.Dashboard={selectedRows,resultView,demoView,recoveryView,DATA};
</script></body></html>
